---
import PageLayout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Hero2 from '~/components/widgets/Hero2.astro';
import TextSplit from '~/components/widgets/TextSplit.astro';
import CTABanner from '~/components/widgets/CTABanner.astro';
import Text from '~/components/ui/Text.astro';
import Heading from '~/components/ui/Heading.astro';
import { getSanityAboutImages } from '~/lib/content/sanity';

const aboutImages = await getSanityAboutImages();

const metadata = {
  title: 'About Aloha Salads | Our Story & Local Sourcing on Oahu',
  description:
    'Learn about Aloha Salads. Founded in Kailua in 2006, we serve fresh, locally sourced food across six Oahu locations. Read our story.',
  ignoreTitleTemplate: true,
};
---

<PageLayout metadata={metadata}>
  {/* ── Page hero ─────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <Hero2
    variant="split-dark"
    overlapHeader={false}
    title="About Aloha Salads"
    subtitle="Fresh From Hawaii. Rooted in Aloha."
    image={aboutImages.hero}
    imageFit="contain"
  />

  {/* ── 1. Our Mission ────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <TextSplit heading="Our Mission">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-accent pl-6">
        <Text variant="body-lg" color="default" class="italic">
          "Aloha Salads was established to serve fresh, locally grown food of the highest quality at affordable prices.
          We remain dedicated to supporting local farmers and fishermen while providing our customers with fresh and
          delicious ingredients."
        </Text>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </TextSplit>

  {/* ── 2. Our Story ──────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <TextSplit heading="Our Story" withImage image={aboutImages.story} imageAspect="4 / 5" class="bg-card">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <Text variant="body-lg" color="default">
        It started with a simple idea: Hawaii deserved a place where eating healthy could be fresh, delicious and
        convenient.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="body" color="default">
        In May 2006 we opened the doors to our first Aloha Salads in Kailua, bringing locally grown ingredients to our
        community. What started as a small family business quickly became a neighborhood favorite.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="body" color="default">
        Since then we have opened at Kahala Mall, Kapolei Commons, Pearlridge Center, Windward Mall in Kaneohe and
        Mililani Town Center. The menu has grown over those twenty years, but the dishes people come back for have not
        changed. The Aloha Passion and the Ono Island Ahi have been on it since the start.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="body" color="default">
        Twenty years later, our mission remains the same. We are proud to serve food made with quality ingredients,
        support local farmers and fishermen, and bring a little more aloha to every meal.
      </Text>
      <Text variant="body" color="default">
        Today, with six locations across Oahu, Aloha Salads is still a family affair. Our roots are in Kailua, our heart
        is in Hawaii, and we are committed to keeping fresh, healthy and affordable food accessible to everyone.
      </Text>
      <Text
        variant="body"
        color="default"
        html="We are honored to be recognized as <strong>First Place, Hawaii's Best 2024, People's Choice Awards, Star-Advertiser</strong>."
      />
    </div>
  </TextSplit>

  {/* ── 3. Founder Story ──────────────────────────────────── */}
  <section class="not-prose w-full bg-section-grey">
    <div
      class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-container flex-col gap-8 px-5 py-12 sm:px-8 md:px-16 md:py-16 lg:px-[120px] lg:py-[120px]"
    >
      <div class="flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-4">
        <Heading variant="h2">Founder Story</Heading>
        <Heading variant="eyebrow">From a Simple Idea to a Family Legacy</Heading>
      </div>
      <div class="flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-6">
        <Text variant="body-lg" color="default">
          Twenty years ago, Sara Lufrano moved back home to Hawaii after living in Chicago. She missed being able to
          grab a fresh, healthy salad on the go, and at the time there wasn't much like it here. So she and her husband
          asked themselves, why don't we create it ourselves?
        </Text>
        <Text variant="body" color="default">
          With a credit card, a lot of hope and plenty of hard work, they opened the very first Aloha Salads in Kailua.
          Living at Sara's parents' house, they stayed up late creating the menu and spent their days chopping, prepping
          and getting everything ready. On opening day it was just the two of them behind the counter. Then came a
          moment they will never forget: a line out the door.
        </Text>
        <Text variant="body" color="default">
          What started as a small idea soon became a family business. Their children grew up in the restaurants, with
          their youngest just a newborn when they opened. Over the years both boys worked alongside their friends,
          becoming part of the family business their parents built from the ground up.
        </Text>
        <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-accent pl-6">
          <Text variant="body-lg" color="default" class="italic">
            "It's wonderful to have the whole family be a part of this business."
          </Text>
          <p class="mt-3 font-heading text-[15px] leading-none text-heading">Sara Lufrano</p>
        </blockquote>
        <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-accent pl-6">
          <Text variant="body-lg" color="default" class="italic">
            "Growing up, the restaurant's always been such a big part of our family. I can't remember a time when it
            wasn't."
          </Text>
          <p class="mt-3 font-heading text-[15px] leading-none text-heading">Kekoa Lufrano</p>
        </blockquote>
        <Text variant="body" color="default">
          Mahalo for being part of our story. Here's to many more years of sharing fresh food and aloha.
        </Text>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── 4. Sustainability — image left / text right ──────────── */}
  <TextSplit heading="Sustainability" withImage image={aboutImages.sustainability} imageReverse imageAspect="4 / 3">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <Text variant="body-lg" color="default">
        For us, sustainability starts close to home. We buy local every week, not because it is a trend, but because it
        is how we have always believed food should be sourced. We rely on vine-ripe tomatoes from Green Growers, a
        Hauula farm, on a standing weekly order, alongside fresh produce from other Oahu farms. Our menu features fresh,
        local, never-frozen ahi sourced from Garden & Valley Isle Seafood, a Honolulu seafood company that delivers
        straight to our kitchens.
      </Text>
      <Text
        variant="body"
        color="default"
        html="Our salad containers are made from molded fiber with no added PFAS. We also use PLA lids for our soup and bowl containers, PLA cold drink cups and lids, AirCarbon straws, and Karat PLA forks and spoons. Learn more about the materials we use on our <a href='/ingredients'>Ingredients page</a>."
      />
    </div>
  </TextSplit>

  {/* ── 5. Our Vendors — text left / image right ─────────── */}
  <TextSplit heading="Our Vendors" withImage image={aboutImages.vendors} imageAspect="4 / 3" class="bg-section-grey">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <Text variant="body-lg" color="default">
        Every delivery of our local ahi carries strict traceability, including lot numbers, an origin of USA wild catch,
        and the named vessel that landed it.
      </Text>
      <Text
        variant="body"
        color="default"
        html="Our long-standing relationships with suppliers and farms such as Green Growers Inc, Ho Farms, Garden & Valley Isle Seafood and Oribe Tea Co help us trace key ingredients back to their sources, from produce grown on Oahu farms to the local ahi we serve. Learn more about where our ingredients come from on our <a href='/ingredients'>Ingredients Page</a>."
      />
    </div>
  </TextSplit>

  {/* ── Find a Location CTA ───────────────────────────────── */}
  <CTABanner
    title="Visit Your Local Restaurant"
    subtitle="Stop by one of our six neighborhood spots across the island for a fresh meal."
    ctaText="Find a Location"
    ctaHref="/locations"
  />
</PageLayout>
